    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="0859" n="739" xml:id="pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.11212/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at
                        Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Blake</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-21T14:00:00+00:00">February 21, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 21—10:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Referring to my telegram No. 1 of January 20, noon.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d792-f1"/> French Resident General, by note dated February 20, 1930,
                    informs me that enforcement of Vizirial Decree of July 6, 1929, concerning
                    stamping of metal containers of imported foodstuffs is postponed for 6 months as
                    from original date of application.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blake</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
